  "summary_en": "Journal article proposing a conceptual design for a software module enabling a geriatric care robot to make moral decisions. It critiques top-down and bottom-up machine-ethics approaches and advocates a hybrid approach based on Nussbaum's capabilities view, using user value profiles elicited through scenarios.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Bottom-up moral learning raises operationalization, transparency and safety problems for care contexts.",
   "The Andersons' top-down approach is unsuited to care requirements; a hybrid approach is better.",
   "Nussbaum's capabilities approach provides the framework for identifying relevant moral values.",
   "Implementation steps: elicit values via interviews, operationalize scenarios, build algorithms, train a user value profile.",
   "Typical conflicts: autonomy versus health, privacy versus health."
